# OpenSpec: Fix TimelineChart sgv/mbg field names → canonical value field (kdiab-5ie)

## Goal
The BFF timeline chart shows no CGM line and no BGM dots because `TimelineChart.tsx` reads
`m.data['sgv']` and `m.data['mbg']` — Nightscout field names — from measure data. Seed data was
normalised to the canonical kdiab schema (`value`/`unit`/`trend`) as part of the kdiab-e99 fix,
but the frontend chart was not updated. This is the frontend counterpart of kdiab-ko5 (backend
AnalyticsService). Additionally, the unit conversion logic uses the JWT `glucoseUnit` claim to
decide whether to treat the stored value as mmol/L, but stored values are always mg/dL — the
`unit` field in `data` is authoritative and should drive conversion instead.

## Context

### File: `kdiab-bff/frontend/src/features/timeline/TimelineChart.tsx`

**CGM block (lines 54–67):**
```typescript
const cgmData = measures
  .filter(m => m.type === 'CGM')
  .map(m => ({
    ts: new Date(m.measuredAt).getTime(),
    sgv: (() => {
      const raw = m.data['sgv'];           // ← reads wrong key
      const val = typeof raw === 'number' ? raw : typeof raw === 'string' ? parseFloat(raw) : NaN;
      if (isNaN(val)) return undefined;
      const mgDl = toMgDl(val, glucoseUnit);   // ← converts using JWT claim, not data.unit
      return displayValue(mgDl, glucoseUnit);
    })(),
  }))
  .filter(d => d.sgv !== undefined)
  .sort((a, b) => a.ts - b.ts);
```

**BGM block (lines 70–82):**
```typescript
const bgmData = measures
  .filter(m => m.type === 'BGM')
  .map(m => ({
    ts: new Date(m.measuredAt).getTime(),
    bgm: (() => {
      const raw = m.data['mbg'];           // ← reads wrong key
      ...
      const mgDl = toMgDl(val, glucoseUnit);   // ← same unit issue
      ...
    })(),
  }))
  .filter(d => d.bgm !== undefined);
```

**Recharts Line (line 126):** `dataKey="sgv"` — must match the mapped property name.

**Unit conversion helpers (lines 37–44):**
```typescript
function toMgDl(value: number, unit: string): number {
  return unit === 'mmol/L' ? value * 18.0 : value;
}
function displayValue(mgDl: number, unit: string): number {
  return unit === 'mmol/L' ? Math.round(mgDl * MGDL_TO_MMOL * 10) / 10 : Math.round(mgDl);
}
```
`toMgDl` is called with `glucoseUnit` (user preference) rather than the measure's own `data.unit`.
Since all stored values are in mg/dL (seed data normalisation), this currently multiplies mg/dL
values by 18 for mmol/L users — producing wildly wrong results. Fix: read `data['unit']` to
determine storage unit; use `glucoseUnit` only for display conversion.

## Interface Changes
No interface changes — pure frontend fix.

## Implementation Plan

**Step 1** — `kdiab-bff/frontend/src/features/timeline/TimelineChart.tsx`:

Replace the CGM mapping block: read `m.data['value']` instead of `m.data['sgv']`; extract storage
unit from `m.data['unit']` (default `'mg/dL'`); use `toMgDl(val, storageUnit)` to normalise to
mg/dL; use `displayValue(mgDl, glucoseUnit)` to convert to display unit. Rename the mapped
property from `sgv` to `value`.

```typescript
const cgmData = measures
  .filter(m => m.type === 'CGM')
  .map(m => ({
    ts: new Date(m.measuredAt).getTime(),
    value: (() => {
      const raw = m.data['value'];
      const val = typeof raw === 'number' ? raw : typeof raw === 'string' ? parseFloat(raw) : NaN;
      if (isNaN(val)) return undefined;
      const storageUnit = typeof m.data['unit'] === 'string' ? m.data['unit'] as string : 'mg/dL';
      const mgDl = toMgDl(val, storageUnit);
      return displayValue(mgDl, glucoseUnit);
    })(),
  }))
  .filter(d => d.value !== undefined)
  .sort((a, b) => a.ts - b.ts);
```

**Step 2** — Same file: replace the BGM mapping block analogously (`m.data['mbg']` →
`m.data['value']`; storage unit from `m.data['unit']`; rename local property from `bgm` to
`bgmValue` to avoid conflict with the `value` key).

```typescript
const bgmData = measures
  .filter(m => m.type === 'BGM')
  .map(m => ({
    ts: new Date(m.measuredAt).getTime(),
    bgmValue: (() => {
      const raw = m.data['value'];
      const val = typeof raw === 'number' ? raw : typeof raw === 'string' ? parseFloat(raw) : NaN;
      if (isNaN(val)) return undefined;
      const storageUnit = typeof m.data['unit'] === 'string' ? m.data['unit'] as string : 'mg/dL';
      const mgDl = toMgDl(val, storageUnit);
      return displayValue(mgDl, glucoseUnit);
    })(),
  }))
  .filter(d => d.bgmValue !== undefined);
```

**Step 3** — Same file: update Recharts components to use new property names:
- `<Line dataKey="sgv"` → `<Line dataKey="value"`
- `<Scatter dataKey="bgm"` → `<Scatter dataKey="bgmValue"`

## Test Plan
- [ ] Frontend build: `cd kdiab-bff/frontend && npm run build` — TypeScript compile clean, no errors
- [ ] Manual smoke (if app is running): log in as sarah/mike, navigate to Timeline — CGM line
  and BGM dots are visible in the chart for the selected timeframe
- [ ] Quality gate: `npm run lint` passes

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] CGM glucose line is rendered in the timeline chart for users with seeded data
- [ ] BGM dots are rendered for users with seeded BGM data
- [ ] For mmol/L users (mike), values are divided by 18 for display, not multiplied
- [ ] `npm run build` passes with no TypeScript errors

## Risks & Assumptions
- All seed data stores values in mg/dL regardless of user preference — `data.unit` is always
  `"mg/dL"` in the current seed. The fix is correct and forward-compatible: if a future source
  stores mmol/L, `data.unit` will be `"mmol/L"` and `toMgDl` will correctly multiply by 18.
- No backend changes needed — the BFF passes `data` as an opaque `JsonObject`; the field name
  issue is purely in the frontend extraction.
- No OpenAPI changes — the `data` field is typed as `object` / `Record<string, unknown>`.

# OpenSpec: Fix timeline tooltips dark theme + BGM scatter detail (kdiab-d9aw + kdiab-cr5p)

## Goal
kdiab-d9aw: Recharts Tooltip contentStyle with CSS custom properties (var(--tooltip-bg)) does not reliably resolve in Recharts inline style context causing white background. Replace with custom content= React component using CSS classes.
kdiab-cr5p: BGM Scatter hover shows only a bare numeric Y value; treatment Scatter hover shows meaningless position. The custom tooltip component will show proper labels for each series type.

## Context
- kdiab-ui/src/features/timeline/TimelineChart.tsx lines 135-140: <Tooltip labelFormatter formatter contentStyle wrapperStyle>.
- BGM data shape: { ts, bgmValue } — no source/unit in tooltip payload.
- Treatment data shape: { ts, y, type, notes } — y is tirHigh + 10 (position), not a meaningful value.
- kdiab-ui/src/index.css: --tooltip-bg, --tooltip-text, --tooltip-border defined. No .timeline-tooltip class.

## Interface Changes
None.

## Implementation Plan
1. kdiab-ui/src/features/timeline/TimelineChart.tsx:
   - Add TimelineTooltip component above TimelineChart:

     interface TtPayload { dataKey: string; value: number; payload: Record<string, unknown> }
     function TimelineTooltip({ active, payload, label, glucoseUnit }: {
       active?: boolean; payload?: TtPayload[]; label?: number; glucoseUnit: string
     }) {
       if (!active || !payload?.length || label == null) return null
       const yUnit = glucoseUnit === "mmol/L" ? "mmol/L" : "mg/dL"
       return (
         <div className="timeline-tooltip">
           <p className="timeline-tooltip-time">{new Date(label).toLocaleString()}</p>
           {payload.map((p, i) => {
             if (p.dataKey === "value") return <p key={i}><strong>CGM</strong> {p.value} {yUnit}</p>
             if (p.dataKey === "bgmValue") return <p key={i}><strong>BGM</strong> {p.value} {yUnit}</p>
             if (p.dataKey === "y") {
               const type = p.payload["type"] as string ?? ""
               const notes = p.payload["notes"] as string | undefined
               return <p key={i}><strong>{type}</strong>{notes ? " — " + notes : ""}</p>
             }
             return null
           })}
         </div>
       )
     }

   - Replace <Tooltip labelFormatter formatter contentStyle wrapperStyle> with:
     <Tooltip content={(props) => <TimelineTooltip {...props} glucoseUnit={glucoseUnit} />} />

2. kdiab-ui/src/index.css — add CSS classes:
   .timeline-tooltip {
     background: var(--tooltip-bg);
     border: 1px solid var(--tooltip-border);
     border-radius: 8px;
     color: var(--tooltip-text);
     padding: 8px 12px;
     font-size: 0.85rem;
     line-height: 1.6;
     max-width: 260px;
     pointer-events: none;
   }
   .timeline-tooltip-time {
     color: var(--text-secondary);
     font-size: 0.8rem;
     margin-bottom: 4px;
   }

## Test Plan
- [ ] Visual: hover CGM line -> dark tooltip showing time + CGM value + unit
- [ ] Visual: hover BGM dot -> dark tooltip showing time + BGM value + unit
- [ ] Visual: hover treatment triangle -> dark tooltip showing type and notes
- [ ] npm run build passes

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Tooltip background is dark (matches app theme)
- [ ] BGM hover shows glucose value and unit
- [ ] Treatment hover shows type label and notes
- [ ] npm run build passes

## Risks & Assumptions
- Recharts content prop completely replaces default tooltip rendering — all formatting must move into TimelineTooltip.
- payload[0].payload holds the raw data object — type and notes fields accessible from there.

